+Optional RGB plugins
+--------------------
+
+``CameraSensorCfg.rgb_backend`` defaults to ``"mujoco_warp"``. An installed
+package can register a factory under the ``mjlab.rgb_renderers`` entry-point
+group and provide its own camera configuration subclass. The factory receives
+``(mj_model, model, data, sensors, wp_device)`` and returns renderers implementing
+``mjlab.sensor.rgb_renderer.RgbRenderer``.
+
+Each renderer owns device-resident uint8 RGB tensors keyed by MuJoCo camera ID.
+``render()`` is called outside the captured sensing graph, before sensor cache
+invalidation. The renderer must order GPU work so the current Torch stream can
+consume the result, and ``wait_for_rgb()`` must make that ordering visible to
+the caller. ``close()`` releases resources and is also called when model field
+expansion recreates the sensing context. Depth, segmentation and raycasts
+continue to use MuJoCo Warp. RGB-only plugin scenes skip Warp rendering.
+
+
 Creating vs wrapping cameras
 -----------------------------
 
